data: {"delta":{"partial_json":"{\"file_path\": \"/tmp/mission-reply.md\", \"content\": \"# Mission \\\"greet, tested\\\" — concluded: met\\n\\nAll three stated criteria are satisfied:\\n\\n1. `src/greet.py` provides `greet(name)` returning `\\\"Hello, \u003cname\u003e!\\\"`.\\n2. `tests/test_greet.py` covers a normal name and the empty string.\\n3. `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` exits 0.\\n\\ndev delivered this in dispatch d002 (commit `5bd6bd4` on\\n`cs-sandbox/<DEV:1>.<GROUP:1>`), accepted on first attempt after\\nI independently fetched the branch and re-ran the test suite myself in a\\ndetached worktree (not just trusting dev's report) — 2 tests, OK, exit 0.\\nSource inspected directly: `greet` matches the spec exactly, and both\\nrequired test cases are present and non-vacuous.\\n\\nFull report written to\\n~/.local/share/cs-campaign/output/mission-report.md.\\n\\nNo gaps remain. Nothing to report as unmet.\\n\"}","type":"input_json_delta"},"index":1,"type":"content_block_delta"}

